# Project architecture

## What this repo is

Automated Austrian embassy appointment booking: n8n watches slots, Python booker submits via Playwright.

## Repo layout (source of truth)

```
files/
├── n8n/                          # Canonical workflow exports (booker, watcher)
├── python-booker-webhook/        # FastAPI + Playwright booker service
│   ├── app.py                    # Production entry: uvicorn app:app
│   ├── booker_legacy.py          # Shared core + legacy wizard (monolith — shrink, don't grow)
│   ├── captcha_ocr.py            # OCR client (candidate for booker/ package)
│   ├── scheduler_html.py         # Pure HTML parsing (candidate for booker/ package)
│   ├── tests/unit|integration|e2e/
│   ├── fixtures/payloads/        # Canonical test JSON (not docs/, not repo root)
│   ├── scripts/                  # Operational CLIs (scan, run payload, OCR check)
│   ├── sandboxes/                # Lock/OCR experiments — workflows + scripts ONLY
│   └── artifacts/                # Gitignored runtime output
└── archive/                      # Retired docs/CSVs
```

## Runtime flow

1. **Watcher** (n8n) scans BMEIA scheduler → writes pending slots
2. **Booker** (n8n) merges student + slot → `POST /webhook/booker`
3. **Turbo path** (`app.py`): scheduler POST → captcha (OCR/Gemini) → Playwright submit (~6–12s)
4. **Legacy path** (`/webhook/booker-legacy`): full Playwright wizard (~26s)

## VPS services

| Port | Service |
|------|---------|
| 8000 | `uvicorn app:app` — booker webhook |
| 8001 | OCR `/predict` (separate captcha_recognition service) |

## Where things belong

| Add this | Put it here |
|----------|-------------|
| Unit test | `tests/unit/test_*.py` |
| FastAPI smoke test | `tests/integration/` |
| Playwright live test | `tests/e2e/` |
| Test payload JSON | `fixtures/payloads/` |
| n8n workflow export | `n8n/` (+ optional copy in `workflows/`) |
| One-off VPS debug | `scripts/debug/` (gitignored) |
| Architecture doc | `docs/` |
| Ephemeral scan output | Nowhere in git — `artifacts/` or delete |

